From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] emulator: let one emulator serve several modems

An emulator belongs to one modem: ofono_emulator_create(modem, type)
adds a single EMULATOR_HFP or EMULATOR_DUN atom and the link goes down
with it. hfp_ag_bluez5 therefore picks one voicecall capable modem for
each headset, the first one with a ready SIM, and a dual-SIM phone only
ever shows the headset the calls of that one. On the mindphone (MT6739,
two SIMs) a call on /ril_0 reached the phone but never the Nuraphone:
no RING, no +CIEV, no +CLCC.

Take the API from Sailfish OS oFono d9c68c4f ("[ofono] Support multiple
modems in emulator. JB#42297", Juho Hämäläinen):
ofono_emulator_create(type) makes the emulator, and
ofono_emulator_add_modem(em, modem) gives it one atom on each modem it
serves. ofono_emulator_register() registers all of them; a modem added
to a link that is already up is registered straight away, and adding a
modem twice does nothing. The link stays up while any of its atoms is
registered and is torn down with the last one, so a modem going away no
longer takes the headset with it. The emulator is freed with its last
atom.

The call lookup for +CLIP and RING now searches the voicecall atom of
every modem. Sailfish stops at the first modem that has a voicecall
atom, which misses a call on the second SIM; this does not.

hfp_ag_bluez5, dun_gw_bluez5 and examples/emulator.c create the
emulator and add the one modem they used before, so nothing changes
for them yet; DUN stays a single-modem service. 0123 gives the HFP
emulator every voice capable modem.

The command handlers and the call indicators are still shared by all
modems here, as in Sailfish; the next two patches give them per-modem
state.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/examples/emulator.c b/examples/emulator.c
index 927cf1f..7a59f25 100644
--- a/examples/emulator.c
+++ b/examples/emulator.c
@@ -110,10 +110,11 @@ static gboolean on_socket_connected(GIOChannel *chan, GIOCondition cond,
 
 	DBG("Picked modem %p for emulator", modem);
 
-	em = ofono_emulator_create(modem, GPOINTER_TO_INT(user));
+	em = ofono_emulator_create(GPOINTER_TO_INT(user));
 	if (!em)
 		goto error;
 
+	ofono_emulator_add_modem(em, modem);
 	ofono_emulator_register(em, fd);
 	return TRUE;
 
